<%# Explains how to read the pie: portions of one whole, not grades. %>
<div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/50 p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
  <p class="font-semibold text-ink">How to read the pie</p>
  <p class="text-mute mt-1">Think of this as one whole — <em>you</em> — cut into portions. A bigger slice doesn't mean you passed and a smaller one doesn't mean you failed. It means you currently have <span class="text-ink">greater capacity</span> in the bigger slices (they come easily, they energize you, you'd do them for free) and <span class="text-ink">smaller capacity</span> in the smaller ones — usually because that's not where your interest lives yet, or because it's simply unexplored. Nobody's pie is all one color. The larger slices point to where you'll thrive on a team right now; the smaller ones are options, not obligations — and any of them can grow if you decide you want it to.</p>
</div>
